# Emeq Hub × DataForSEO — fase 2: Consumer-contract via de Hub
#
# Test /v1/dataforseo/* (Bearer PAT + X-Account-Id). Draai eerst fase 1:
# partner/domain-overview.http (direct naar api.dataforseo.com).
#
# Vereist de Hub-code op branch agent/open-seo (of na merge daarvan).
#
# ── Setup ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Fase 1 groen: partner-API werkt (account geverifieerd bij DataForSEO).
# 2. Hub: HUB_PROVIDER_DATAFORSEO_ENABLED=true in root-.env; Connection met
#    login:password voor het Account (admin of POST /v1/connections).
# 3. PAT met ability `dataforseo:read` (of `*`) in docs/dataforseo/.env:
#      VS Code:  EMEQ_HUB_PAT=1|…
#      PhpStorm: http-client.private.env.json → token, Run with "local"
#
# 4. X-Account-Id = `external_id` van het Account (niet het interne id).
#
# Conventie: één .http-bestand per partner in deze map. Zie README.md.

@baseUrl = http://hub.emeq.test:8092
@token = {{$dotenv EMEQ_HUB_PAT}}
@accountId = 47
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/dataforseo/domain-overview?domain=example.com
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
X-Account-Id: {{accountId}}
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/dataforseo/domain-overview?domain=example.com&location_name=Netherlands
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
X-Account-Id: {{accountId}}
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/dataforseo/domain-overview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
X-Account-Id: {{accountId}}
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/dataforseo/domain-overview?domain=example.com
Accept: application/json
X-Account-Id: {{accountId}}